# PMC — RPKI invalid prefixes
# Canvas: pmc | Collection: pmc.prefixes
# Description: Surface RPKI-invalid route announcements from peers

# Prompt: show rpki invalid prefixes
# Prompt: list rpki invalid routes
# Prompt: which peers have invalid rpki
# Prompt: show prefixes with invalid roa
# Prompt: find rpki violations
# The lines above are paraphrases of ONE question for the NL widget. The IQE below
# is what the pmc adapter answers it with (tools/iqe/adapters/pmc.py).
foreach x in pmc.prefixes
where x.rpki_status == "invalid"
select x.prefix, x.origin_asn, x.rpki_status, x.asn, x.org_name
# Not applied: IQE has no `order by`, so the executor returns every matching row, unsorted and uncapped. Intended presentation, not performed: sort by x.asn.
